{"toolCallId":"call_d3356e444ba14201923b934915ed1303","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n<!-- FILL: Keep the prefix table and add the two shell variables this task list uses. GOOD: `S` is the script path. `P` is the packet path. WEAK: Variables are defined below. -->\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n<!-- FILL: Replace the sample tasks with the real setup steps. Each task names a file and a verify command. GOOD: T001 Read the output block in `recommend-level.sh`. Verify: `rg -n 'Recommended Level'` prints one line. WEAK: T001 Set up the project. -->\n\n- [ ] T001 Create project structure (`<folder>`). Verify: `ls <folder>` lists it.\n- [ ] T002 Install dependencies (`<manifest>`). Verify: `<install command>` exits 0.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Configure development tools (`<config>`). Verify: `<tool> --version` exits 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n<!-- FILL: Write one implementation task per file change. Add a `Verify:` line with the command and its expected output. GOOD: T002 Add the `--quiet` branch. Verify: `--quiet` prints one line. WEAK: T002 Implement the feature. -->\n\n- [ ] T004 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 1]\n- [ ] T005 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 2]\n- [ ] T006 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 3]\n- [ ] T007 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Add error handling]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n<!-- FILL: Write one verification task per requirement. Each one runs a command. GOOD: T003 Run both invocations. Verify: `wc -l` prints 1 and 17. WEAK: T003 Test everything. -->\n\n- [ ] T008 Test happy path manually (`<file>`). Verify: `<command>` prints <expected output>.\n- [ ] T009 Test edge cases (`<test>`). Verify: `<test command>` exits 0.\n- [ ] T010 Update documentation (`<doc>`). Verify: `rg -n '<term>' <doc>` prints one line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n<!-- FILL: Keep the three completion lines and add the one artifact that proves the phase is done. GOOD: `--quiet` prints one line and the suite passes. WEAK: Work is complete. -->\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n<!-- FILL: Name the spec and plan files. Add the decision record when the packet has one. GOOD: Specification: `spec.md`. Plan: `plan.md`. WEAK: See the other docs. -->\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n<!-- FILL: Fill each checklist section below. GOOD: Each CHK line names the command that answers it. WEAK: The checklist is done. -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n<!-- FILL: Keep the three rows and add the rule this packet uses for a blocked task. GOOD: P0 blocks close. P1 needs a recorded reason. WEAK: Follow the priorities. -->\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per setup fact, each with a command. GOOD: CHK-001 [P0] The start commit is in `goal.md` section 4. WEAK: Setup is ready. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per file rule. A command must answer it. GOOD: CHK-010 [P0] `bash -n recommend-level.sh` exits 0. WEAK: Code is clean. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] Code passes lint/format checks\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No console errors or warnings\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Error handling implemented\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] Code follows project patterns\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per acceptance criterion. GOOD: CHK-020 [P0] `--quiet` prints one line. WEAK: Tests pass. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] Manual testing complete\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Edge cases tested\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Error scenarios validated\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n<!-- FILL: Keep this section, because every level requires it. Write one check per finding class this packet can produce. Delete only the rows that do not apply, never the section. GOOD: CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Every finding names one class. WEAK: All findings handled. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each actionable finding has a finding class: `instance-only`, `class-of-bug`, `cross-consumer`, `algorithmic`, `matrix/evidence`, or `test-isolation`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed, or instance-only status proven by grep.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed for changed helpers, policies, schema fields, response fields, docs, and tests.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] Security/path/parser/redaction fixes include adversarial table tests for delimiter, joined-input, outside-root, no-op, and fallback cases.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count are listed before completion is claimed.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Hostile env/global-state variant executed when tests or code read process-wide state.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence is pinned to a fix SHA or explicit diff range, not a moving branch-relative range.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per security surface. Write `N/A` with a reason when none applies. GOOD: CHK-030 [P0] The script reads no credential. WEAK: Security is fine. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation implemented\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] Auth/authz working correctly\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per document that must agree. GOOD: CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md` and `tasks.md` name the same flag. WEAK: Docs are updated. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec/plan/tasks synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] Code comments adequate\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] README updated (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per file location rule. GOOD: CHK-050 [P1] Test copies live under `scratch/test/`. WEAK: Files are organized. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temp files in scratch/ only\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] scratch/ cleaned before completion\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n<!-- FILL: Count the boxes by priority and write the three totals. GOOD: P0 12, P1 13, P2 1. WEAK: Most items done. -->\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | [X] | [ ]/[X] |\n| P1 Items | [Y] | [ ]/[Y] |\n| P2 Items | [Z] | [ ]/[Z] |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-26\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per ADR, or delete the section when the packet records no ADR. GOOD: CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 is followed by T002. WEAK: Architecture is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] Architecture decisions documented in decision-record.md\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] All ADRs have status (Proposed/Accepted)\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives documented with rejection rationale\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] Migration path documented (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per performance claim, or delete the section when the packet makes none. GOOD: CHK-110 [P1] The flag adds under 5 ms. WEAK: Performance is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] Response time targets met (NFR-P01)\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P1] Throughput targets met (NFR-P02)\n- [ ] CHK-112 [P2] Load testing completed\n- [ ] CHK-113 [P2] Performance benchmarks documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per deployment step, or delete the section when the packet ships no service. GOOD: CHK-120 [P0] The rollback command was run in a copy. WEAK: Ready to deploy. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented and tested\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P0] Feature flag configured (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-122 [P1] Monitoring/alerting configured\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P1] Runbook created\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] Deployment runbook reviewed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per compliance surface, or delete the section when none applies. GOOD: CHK-130 [P1] No license changed. WEAK: Compliance is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] Security review completed\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] Dependency licenses compatible\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] OWASP Top 10 checklist completed\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] Data handling compliant with requirements\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per document pair that must agree, or delete the section when the packet holds no paired documents. GOOD: CHK-140 [P1] `plan.md` and `tasks.md` agree on the three phases. WEAK: Docs are verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] API documentation complete (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Name the real approver for each role. Delete a row when the role does not exist. Write `N/A` or delete the section when no sign-off applies. GOOD: Conductor, runs every task. Operator, merges the commit. WEAK: Signed off. -->\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Technical Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Product Owner | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | QA Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\nTwo shell variables keep the lines short. Export both before running any Verify command:\n\n```bash\nS=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nP=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n```\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ai-execution -->\n## AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL\n\n### Pre-Task Checklist\n1. Read `spec.md` and confirm the requirement you are implementing is in scope\n2. Read `plan.md` and confirm the phase you are in\n3. Find the next uncompleted task in this file and confirm its dependencies are done\n4. Confirm the baseline files exist in `$P/scratch/` before touching the script\n5. Confirm you are editing only `recommend-level.sh`\n\n### Execution Rules\n\n| Rule | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| TASK-SEQ | Run tasks in id order; do not start Phase 3 before Phase 2 is complete |\n| TASK-SCOPE | Edit `recommend-level.sh` only; no other file, no spec-doc rewrite |\n| TASK-VERIFY | Run the Verify command for a task before marking it `[x]` |\n| TASK-REPORT | After each task, report the task id, the files touched and the Verify output |\n\n### Status Reporting Format\n`T0NN complete. File: recommend-level.sh. Verify: <command> printed <output>.`\n\n### Blocked Task Protocol\nIf a Verify command prints something other than its expected output: stop, mark the task `[B]`, record the command and the observed output in `$P/scratch/`, and report the blocker instead of editing around it.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ai-execution -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the parser, the output functions and the help text (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'output_text\\(\\)|output_json\\(\\)|show_help\\(\\)' \"$S\"` prints the three definitions.\n- [ ] T002 Capture the default output for the four fixtures (`$P/scratch/`). Verify: `wc -l \"$P\"/scratch/baseline-f*.txt` prints 16, 16, 17 and 17.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T003 Add `QUIET=false` to the globals block (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n '^QUIET=false$' \"$S\"` prints one line.\n- [ ] T004 Add the `--quiet` case to the argument parser, next to the other boolean flags (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n '^    --quiet\\)' \"$S\"` prints one line.\n- [ ] T005 Add `output_quiet()` beside `output_text()`, printing `Recommended Level: ${RECOMMENDED_LEVEL} (${LEVEL_NAME})` (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n '^output_quiet\\(\\)' \"$S\"` prints one line.\n- [ ] T006 Dispatch quiet before JSON and text in the output section (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc 60 --files 3 | wc -l` prints 1.\n- [ ] T007 Add the guard that rejects `--quiet` with `--json` after input validation (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --json --loc 60 --files 3 >/dev/null 2>&1; echo $?` prints 1.\n- [ ] T008 Document the flag in the header OPTIONS block and in `show_help` (`$S`). Verify: `rg -c -- '--quiet' \"$S\"` prints 3.\n- [ ] T009 Run the syntax check (`$S`). Verify: `bash -n \"$S\"` exits 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T010 Prove the one-line contract on all four fixtures (`$S`). Verify: `for a in \"--loc 60 --files 3\" \"--loc 200 --files 5 --api\" \"--loc 600 --files 12 --api --db\" \"--loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural\"; do bash \"$S\" --quiet $a | wc -l; done` prints `1` four times.\n- [ ] T011 Prove the quiet label is exact (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural` prints `Recommended Level: 3 (Full)`.\n- [ ] T012 Prove the default report is unchanged (`$S`). Verify: `diff \"$P/scratch/baseline-f1.txt\" <(bash \"$S\" --loc 60 --files 3)` prints nothing, and the same for F2-F4.\n- [ ] T013 Prove quiet and default agree on the level (`$S`). Verify: `for a in \"--loc 60 --files 3\" \"--loc 200 --files 5 --api\" \"--loc 600 --files 12 --api --db\" \"--loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural\"; do [ \"$(bash \"$S\" --quiet $a)\" = \"$(bash \"$S\" $a | rg '^Recommended Level:')\" ] || echo \"MISMATCH: $a\"; done` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T014 Prove the error paths keep their messages and exit codes (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --json --loc 60 --files 3 2>&1 >/dev/null` prints `ERROR: --quiet and --json cannot be combined`, and `bash \"$S\" --quiet` exits 1.\n- [ ] T015 Prove help still prints in full under `--quiet` (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --help | rg -n '^  --quiet'` prints one line and the command exits 0.\n- [ ] T016 Run the existing regression suite (`runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-system.sh`). Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-system.sh` prints `12 passed, 0 failed`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] `$P/acceptance-criteria.md` has no `Unmet` row\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n\nA `[B]` task blocks its phase: no later task starts until the blocker is recorded and cleared.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md. Verify: `rg -c '^\\| REQ-00' \"$P/spec.md\"` prints 8.\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md. Verify: `rg -c '^### ADR-00' \"$P/plan.md\"` prints 2.\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available. Verify: `bash --version` exits 0 and prints a 3.2+ version.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] The script parses. Verify: `bash -n \"$S\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] The happy path writes nothing to stderr. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc 60 --files 3 2>&1 >/dev/null | wc -l` prints 0.\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Error handling implemented. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --json --loc 60 --files 3 2>&1 >/dev/null` prints the conflict message.\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The new case matches the surrounding style. Verify: `rg -n '^    --(auth|api|db|quiet)\\)' \"$S\"` prints four case labels in one block.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met. Verify: every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` reads `Met`.\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] Manual testing complete. Verify: T010 and T012 printed their expected output.\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Edge cases tested. Verify: repeated `--quiet`, `--quiet --help` and `--quiet` with no inputs each behave as `spec.md` §8 states.\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Error scenarios validated. Verify: unknown option, non-numeric value and missing inputs each exit 1 with stderr text.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-comple